Chapter 7 — The Personal AI Learning Agent

7.1 Definition

The personal AI learning agent is a persistent, adaptive, multi-modal, teacher-governed intelligent system assigned to one learner.

It is not a chatbot. It is a Personal Educational Intelligence Layer.

7.2 Functions

· Diagnose current state.
· Explain concepts at the learner's level.
· Question to elicit understanding.
· Practice with the learner.
· Assess evidence of mastery.
· Seed new domains.
· Reflect with the learner.
· Report to the teacher.
· Protect the learner's privacy.

7.3 Agent Architecture

```
Student Agent
├── Knowledge
├── Interests
├── Progress
├── Misconceptions
├── Questions
└── Learning Pace
```

7.4 Agent Roles (Multi-Agent)

· Tutor Agent — explains, dialogues.
· Planner Agent — sequences learning.
· Verifier Agent — checks correctness.
· Seeding Agent — proposes new domains.
· Assessment Agent — evaluates evidence.
· Reflection Agent — supports metacognition.

7.5 Example Interaction

Learner: “I don’t understand this equation.”

The agent should not simply provide the answer. It should diagnose.

It may discover that the learner has forgotten:

· fractions;
· algebraic notation;
· proportional reasoning;
· or a prerequisite concept.

The agent then dynamically constructs an appropriate explanation.

7.6 Voice, Text, and Multi-Modality

Interaction supports:

· Text → AI
· Voice → AI
· AI → Voice
· AI → Text
· AI → Visual explanation
· Student → Project

7.7 The Agent as Companion

The agent accompanies the learner across years, not sessions. It remembers:

· what the student has learned;
· what remains difficult;
· what questions have been abandoned;
· what projects were completed;
· what new interests emerged.

This longitudinality is one of the largest potential differences between conventional educational software and persistent AI agents.

