Chapter 11 — Multi-LLM Interoperability

11.1 The Principle

The system should not depend on a single LLM.

\text{Education Platform} \rightarrow \text{LLM Orchestration Layer} \rightarrow \{LLM_1, LLM_2, \ldots, LLM_n\}

11.2 Specialization

Different models may specialize in:

· mathematics;
· programming;
· languages;
· science;
· reasoning;
· tutoring;
· translation;
· speech;
· vision;
· local languages;
· low-cost inference;
· privacy-preserving deployment;
· safety-critical educational functions.

11.3 Orchestration

Example:

\text{Student Agent} \rightarrow \text{Planner LLM} \rightarrow \text{Specialist LLM} \rightarrow \text{Verifier LLM} \rightarrow \text{Teacher Interface}

