17.2 Hypotheses

H1. A persistent learner model + agent improves learning gains compared to an LLM without memory.

H2. A teacher dashboard improves intervention precision and reduces teacher workload.

H3. Knowledge Seeding increases curiosity diversity and depth without reducing foundational mastery.

H4. Open learner model and learner agency increase motivation and self-regulation without reducing curricular coverage.

H5. Governance by design reduces risk without degrading learner experience.

H6. Effects are heterogeneous across learner profiles.

H7. Multi-LLM orchestration improves robustness, cost, and localization compared to single-model deployment.

