APPENDIX G — GLOSSARY OF TERMS

Agentic Education — Educational model in which each learner is accompanied by a persistent AI agent under teacher governance.

AI Agent — A persistent, autonomous, adaptive software system capable of perception, reasoning, and action within a domain.

Cognitive Tutor — An intelligent tutoring system based on cognitive models of learning.

Consent Architecture — Technical and procedural mechanisms ensuring informed, ongoing, and revocable consent.

Curiosity Space — The set of domains, questions, and ideas a learner is currently able to explore or imagine.

Deep Knowledge Tracing (DKT) — Neural network approach to modeling learner knowledge over time.

GAEI — Global Agentic Education Infrastructure.

Knowledge Seeding — Deliberate exposure of learners to domains, concepts, and questions to expand their curiosity space.

Learner State Model — Structured, longitudinal, inspectable representation of a learner's educational state.

LLM — Large Language Model.

Mastery Loop — Observe → Represent → Diagnose → Explain → Practice → Evaluate → Update.

Misconception — A persistent, incorrect understanding that interferes with learning.

Multi-LLM Interoperability — Architectural capacity to use multiple LLM providers interchangeably.

Open Learner Model — A learner model that is visible and editable by the learner.

Personal Educational Intelligence Layer — The persistent AI agent assigned to one learner.

Privacy by Design — Embedding privacy protections into system architecture from the outset.

Socratic Dialogue — Teaching through questioning rather than direct instruction.

Teacher Orchestration — Real-time pedagogical management of multiple AI-mediated learning processes.

Verifier Agent — AI component that checks correctness of generated content.

